  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Cyanide process, which is also known as MacArthur cyanide process involves the extraction of gold and silver from their ores by dissolving them in a dilute solution of sodium cyanide or potassium cyanide.&nbsp;The leaching is carried out in the presence of air or oxygen to oxidise the metal.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi></math> is leached by cyanide process by making the complex using <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>KCN</mi></math> as follows</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ag</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>NaCN</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><munder><mrow><mi>Na</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ag</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>Soluble</mi></munder><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
